abstract = {In this paper, we introduce the notion of subcell resolution, which is based on the observation that unlike point values, cell-averages of a discontinuous piecewise-smooth function contain information about the exact location of the discontinuity within the cell. Using this observation we design an essentially non-oscillatory (ENO) reconstruction technique which is exact for cell averages of discontinuous piecewise-polynomial functions of the appropriate degree. Later on we incorporate this new reconstruction technique into Godunov-type schemes in order to produce a modification of the ENO schemes which prevents the smearing of contact discontinuities.}
}
