author = {Shailesh Kumar Shivakumar},
keywords = {Comprehensive security strategy, security analysis, threat modeling, security design, security implementation, security testing, vulnerabilities, threats, risk assessment, security principles, defense-in-depth security, security policies},
abstract = {Security is a critical requirement for enterprise applications. Some enterprise domains such as finance and retail are more sensitive to security than others. Enterprise application security encompasses a wide range of concerns such as protection of confidential data, prevention of external and internal attacks, adoption of suitable encryption standards, and enforcement of security best practices at hardware and software components and others. Security has a direct impact on the three quality attributes discussed throughout this book. A severe kind of security attack such as distributed denial of service will slow down the application performance and can lead to availability issues. Other adverse impacts of security incidents include material loss, erosion of customer base and loyalty, compromise of intellectual property, and others. Likewise, security is of paramount importance for application availability and performance. We will look at various aspects of security such as the main security concerns for an enterprise application, security guidelines, best practices, and security checklists. Wherever necessary, sample code snippets are also provided. In this chapter, we will look at security principles, best practices, and achieving security at software and infrastructure levels. Wherever necessary, scenarios are explained with code examples.}
}
@incollection{CATHCART2010461,
